OL,3,GNEWSANo unconditional support to arms
OL,4,Aindustry, says Welsh government
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe Plaid Welsh government said it
OL,7,Fwon't give unconditional support to the
OL,8,Fdefence industry - the same day a
OL,9,Fdefence trade show that it has
OL,10,Fsponsored opened in Newport.
OL,12,FIt is drawing up a new ethical policy
OL,13,Fon investing in the sector, a minister
OL,14,Fsaid the administration did not want to
OL,15,Fsupport companies which sell arms to
OL,16,Fcountries "who carry out genocide".
OL,18,FReform accused Plaid of putting its
OL,19,F"political ideology" above thousands of
OL,20,Fjobs, while the Tories described the
OL,21,Fnew policy as an "investment freeze" at
OL,22,Fa dangerous time.
OL,23,APub: 03-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
FL,438,430,260,140,0,100
